 ("A rate is reported as 7 new infections per 1,000 person-years. What does person-time handle?","Different amounts of observation time contributed by participants.",["Differences in test sensitivity only.","Only existing cases at baseline.","The number of clinic visits per case."],"Person-time accommodates unequal follow-up while people remain at risk."),
 ("A disease has many existing cases but few new cases because patients survive for years. Which measure captures this burden?","Prevalence.",["Incidence rate only.","Odds ratio only.","Case-fatality proportion only."],"Prevalence describes the existing burden at a point or over a period."),
