 ("A school-based vaccination program needs parents' trust. Which step is appropriate?","Provide clear information, listen to concerns, and make consent and access processes understandable.",["Dismiss questions as misinformation without discussion.","Hide adverse-event information.","Require participation without explaining the program."],"Transparent engagement supports informed decisions and program trust."),
 ("A program reduces injuries after introducing helmets and safer streets. Which evaluation compares outcomes before and after?","A pre-post evaluation, interpreted cautiously for concurrent changes.",["A case-control study by definition.","A blinded randomized individual trial.","A cross-sectional estimate of sensitivity."],"Pre-post comparison can track change but cannot alone rule out other causes."),
 ("A vaccine adverse event is reported after immunization. What is the correct initial interpretation?","The timing is a signal for assessment, not proof that vaccination caused the event.",["Causation is certain because the event followed vaccination.","The report should always be ignored.","The event proves the vaccine is ineffective."],"Temporal association warrants evaluation using clinical and epidemiologic evidence."),
 ("A community clinic uses reminder texts, walk-in hours, and local outreach. What is this an example of?","A multi-component strategy addressing several access and behavioral barriers.",["A laboratory diagnostic method.","Tertiary prevention only.","A population denominator."],"Combining reminders and convenient delivery can reduce separate barriers to uptake."),
